    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.closeness_vitality - EdgeCase\",\n    \"isPartOf\": {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.closeness_vitality.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.closeness_vitality()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Get closeness vitality centrality for each node.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.closeness_vitality()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Get closeness vitality centrality for each node.\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.closeness_vitality()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n  .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: Get closeness vitality centrality for each node.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nGet closeness vitality centrality for each node.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L65229-L65367){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.closeness_vitality(\n    attr_name=None,\n    return_dict=False,\n    weighted=None,\n)\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![Closeness vitality](../assets/graphs/closeness-vitality.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"The shared seven-node graph shaded by closeness vitality, how much the total pairwise distance drops when a node is removed. Removing the bridge E cuts off the tail, so E tops the table at 66, while the hub C, which the others can route around, scores only 12.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nCloseness vitality is the change in the total distance between all pairs of nodes when\na node is removed:\n\n`vitality(v) = sum_distances(G) - sum_distances(G - v)`\n\nRemoving `v` changes the total in three ways. The distances to and from `v` itself drop\nout, which raises the score of a node that lies far from the rest. Pairs whose shortest\nroute ran through `v` have to detour, which lowers it. And pairs that can no longer\nreach each other at all drop out too, which raises it again. So a node whose loss\nmakes the others take long detours scores low, often below zero, while a node whose\nloss cuts the network apart scores high.\n\nThe sum runs over ordered pairs, so on an undirected graph each pair counts twice, and\nthe scores are twice those of NetworkX. Only finite distances are summed, so every\nscore is finite: NetworkX gives `-inf` to a node whose removal disconnects the graph.\n`node_vitality()` computes the same score for a single node.\n:::\n\n## Parameters {.doc-parameters}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code>[attr_name]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [str | None]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Name for the node attribute to store results. If not provided, auto-generates name from\n    method name (`closeness_vitality`).\n\n<code>[return_dict]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [bool]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[False]{.va}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   If `True`, returns dictionary of results. If `False`, stores results as node attributes\n    and returns self for method chaining.\n\n<code>[weighted]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [bool | None]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   If `True`, measure distances by edge weight (each edge's weight, `1.0` when unset),\n    as in `node_vitality(weighted=True)`. If `False`, count hops. If `None`\n    (default), follows whether the graph was created as weighted.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [Union[dict[int, float], Graph]]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If `return_dict=` is `True`: dictionary mapping node IDs to vitality scores. If\n    `return_dict=` is `False`: returns self for method chaining.\n:::\n\n## Technical Notes {.doc-technical-notes}\n\nCloseness vitality (Koschützki et al., 2005) attributes to each node $v$ the change\nin the graph's *Wiener index* $W(G) = \\sum_{u \\ne w} d(u, w)$ that would result from\nremoving it: $\\mathrm{vit}(v) = W(G) - W(G - v)$. The pairs that include $v$ add\n$\\sum_{u} (d(u, v) + d(v, u))$ to the score, and every other pair subtracts the\namount its distance stretches once $v$ is gone. A pair left without a path drops out\nof $W(G - v)$, since only finite distances are summed, and so adds its old distance\ninstead. The score is negative when the detours outweigh the rest. Computation is\ninherently expensive at $O(V^2 E / p)$ (one all-pairs shortest-path per node,\nparallelized across $p$ cores), so plan on staying below a few thousand nodes;\ndegree, PageRank, or betweenness are the usual proxies at scale.\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~node_vitality`) \n\n:   The same score for a single node.\n\n[](`~closeness_centrality`) \n\n:   How close each node is to the rest.\n\n[](`~betweenness_centrality`) \n\n:   How often each node lies on shortest paths.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nRemoving a leaf of a star drops its own distances from the total, and those of the\nother nodes don't change. Removing the hub drops all its distances, and also those\nbetween the leaves, which can no longer reach each other, so its score is the whole\ntotal:\n\n::: {#9df3ee58 .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\nstar = ec.Graph.from_edges([(\"hub\", \"A\"), (\"hub\", \"B\"), (\"hub\", \"C\")])\n\nlabel = star.get_label_from_id\nvitality = star.closeness_vitality(return_dict=True)\n{label(n): v for n, v in vitality.items()}\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```\n{'B': 10.0, 'hub': 18.0, 'C': 10.0, 'A': 10.0}\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nIn a cycle with a chord, removing an end of the chord makes the others go the long way\naround, and its score falls below the other nodes':\n\n::: {#9f3e3bed .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nring = ec.Graph().add_cycle_graph(8)\nring.add_edge(\"1\", \"5\")\n\nlabel = ring.get_label_from_id\nvitality = ring.closeness_vitality(return_dict=True)\n{label(n): v for n, v in sorted(vitality.items())}\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```\n{'1': -2.0,\n '2': 24.0,\n '3': 30.0,\n '4': 24.0,\n '5': -2.0,\n '6': 24.0,\n '7': 30.0,\n '8': 24.0}\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### Closing a station\n\n`metro()` is a made-up city's metro network, with each track's travel time in minutes\nas its weight. Closing Riverside cuts off the harbor, whose trips then drop out of the\ntotal, so it scores highest. Closing Market forces long detours on the trips that ran\nthrough it, so it scores lowest, far below zero:\n\n::: {#e2f6ee49 .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nmetro = ec.metro()\nvitality = metro.closeness_vitality(return_dict=True)\n\nlabel = metro.get_label_from_id\nranked = sorted(vitality, key=vitality.get)\n[(label(n), vitality[n]) for n in ranked[:2] + ranked[-2:]]\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```\n[('Market', -1142.0),\n ('Old Town', -438.0),\n ('Harbor', 1290.0),\n ('Riverside', 1518.0)]\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n::: {#4acd14d2 .cell execution_count=4}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nmetro.closeness_vitality().plot(\n    layout=\"pos\", color_by=\"closeness_vitality\", color_scale=\"diverging\",\n    label_by=\"label\",\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=4}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-887c9664:#b42318;--ect-687b1aa3:#9fb0c4;--ect-f5c642ae:#d0a195;--ect-6cb1fab5:#c15748;--ect-7a8946be:#d2b0a6;--ect-0e851e70:#d3c9c2;--ect-eacb019e:#ce8f82;--ect-05dd5a64:#d1a498;--ect-03796db1:#bc4637;--ect-deae364a:#d3c5bd;--ect-74ab897e:#cf998c;--ect-0f8cd3fc:#d1aca1;--ect-a7b401b0:#d2b2a8;--ect-24583194:#adb9c6;--ect-5360f3ec:#d3c8c0;--ect-45ce4e0c:#4e7ab5;--ect-fcdc0df1:#d09e91;--ect-c00abef8:#d2b3aa;--ect-f13b2e9c:#c35e4f;--ect-374b3d43:#1c5cab;--ect-7814b41d:#4574b3;--ect-86b8d92a:#688cbb;--ect-ceda7692:#8ba3c1;--ect-983d5a39:#afbac7;--ect-087a119b:#d3d1cb;--ect-044e2c76:#ce9385;--ect-e89136d6:#c87263;--ect-5b7ebd3f:#bf5041;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-978968b0:#7d1810;--ect-61e0bd52:#6f7b89;--ect-362f1d55:#917068;--ect-93b7d88b:#873c32;--ect-74cd6f63:#937b74;--ect-0aee408c:#938c87;--ect-cb1e26f1:#90645b;--ect-3e385a4d:#92726a;--ect-9ef8a57a:#833126;--ect-4fa7f50e:#938984;--ect-d9a1597e:#906b62;--ect-79598845:#927870;--ect-43dbe507:#937c75;--ect-895a67a0:#79818a;--ect-ca6267c9:#938c86;--ect-474f4fb0:#36557e;--ect-d0e2d9dd:#916e65;--ect-4617e3ae:#937d76;--ect-079122f1:#884137;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){.ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-887c9664:#f070